---
/**
 * Project Details Page: Precision Scrollytelling Gallery
 * 
 * This page provides a detailed case study of the Scrollytelling Gallery project.
 * It follows the consistent design pattern used across the portfolio.
 */
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Precision Scrollytelling Gallery Case Study | Jun Alvior';
const description = 'An immersive web experience built with Next.js and Framer Motion. Featuring scroll-driven video assembly sequences and a premium interactive gallery.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
<main id="main-content" class="flex-grow flex flex-col">
      <!-- ORGANISMS: Project Case Study -->
      <article class="py-24 bg-grey-light dark:bg-[#1a1a1a] flex-grow">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
          <!-- Breadcrumb -->
          <div class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
            <a
              href="../../portfolio/"
              class="hover:text-wood-accent transition-colors"
              ><- Back to Portfolio</a
            >
          </div>

          <!-- Header -->
          <header class="mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
            <div class="mb-8 rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
              <img
                src="../../assets/scrollytelling-gallery.png"
                alt="Precision Scrollytelling Gallery"
                class="w-full h-auto object-cover max-h-[500px]"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
                width="800"
                height="450"
              />
            </div>
            <h1
              class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6"
            >
              Precision Scrollytelling Gallery
            </h1>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm">
              <span
                class="px-3 py-1 bg-wood-100 dark:bg-wood-900 text-wood-accent rounded-full font-medium"
                >Next.js 15</span
              >
              <span
                class="px-3 py-1 bg-wood-100 dark:bg-wood-900 text-wood-accent rounded-full font-medium"
                >Framer Motion</span
              >
              <span
                class="px-3 py-1 bg-wood-100 dark:bg-wood-900 text-wood-accent rounded-full font-medium"
                >TypeScript</span
              >
              <span
                class="px-3 py-1 bg-wood-100 dark:bg-wood-900 text-wood-accent rounded-full font-medium"
                >Vanilla CSS</span
              >
            </div>
          </header>

          <!-- Project Links (Top) -->
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mb-12" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="50">
            <a
              href="https://next-js-on-scroll-animation.vercel.app/"
              target="_blank"
              class="px-6 py-3 bg-wood-accent hover:bg-wood-700 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg shadow-md transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 flex items-center"
            >
              <svg
                class="mr-2 w-5 h-5"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="currentColor"
              >
                <path
                  d="M19 19H5V5h7V3H5c-1.11 0-2 .9-2 2v14c0 1.1.89 2 2 2h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2v-7h-2v7zM14 3v2h3.59l-9.83 9.83 1.41 1.41L19 6.41V10h2V3h-7z"
                />
              </svg>
              Live Demo
            </a>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/property360-2/next-js-on-scroll-animation"
              target="_blank"
              class="px-6 py-3 bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-300 dark:hover:bg-gray-700 text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-semibold rounded-lg shadow-md transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 flex items-center"
            >
              <svg
                class="mr-2 w-5 h-5"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="currentColor"
              >
                <path
                  d="M9.4 16.6L4.8 12l4.6-4.6L8 6l-6 6 6 6 1.4-1.4zm5.2 0l4.6-4.6-4.6-4.6L16 6l6 6-6 6-1.4-1.4z"
                />
              </svg>
              View Code
            </a>
          </div>

          <!-- Content -->
          <div
            class="prose dark:prose-invert prose-lg prose-wood max-w-none"
            data-aos="fade-up"
            data-aos-delay="100"
          >
            <h2>Overview</h2>
            <p>
              The Precision Scrollytelling Gallery is a high-performance, immersive web experience that showcases the "Art of Motion." It utilizes scroll-driven video assembly sequences, allowing users to interactively "scrub" through complex breakdowns of mechanical and digital systems.
            </p>

            <h2>The Problem It Solves</h2>
            <p>
              Product showcases and high-end landing pages often struggle to explain intricate mechanical structures or complex assembly steps through standard static images or non-interactive video embeds. This scrollytelling gallery solves this by synchronizing video playback exactly to the user's viewport scrolling speed, enabling users to naturally interact with and inspect complex steps at their own pace with absolute layout precision.
            </p>

            <h3>Key Features</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Smooth Scrollytelling:</strong> Synchronized video playback tied directly to scroll position for a "buttery" feel.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Dynamic Experience Gallery:</strong> A premium grid-based gallery with category filtering and interactive video hover states.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Dynamic Routing:</strong> Automatic page generation for every video experience in the collection.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Ambient UI:</strong> Glassmorphic components, subtle gradients, and staggered entrance animations for a premium feel.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Responsive Optimization:</strong> Tailored for large viewports to preserve high-fidelity interaction models.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Technical Implementation</h3>
            <p>
              Built with the latest <strong>Next.js 15</strong> App Router, the project leverages <strong>Framer Motion</strong> for complex scroll-linked animations. The design system uses modern CSS tokens to achieve a sleek, glassmorphic aesthetic without the overhead of heavy utility frameworks.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ORGANISMS: Footer -->
    </main>
</Layout>
